hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18650","Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Isa ibn Dinar narrated to us, my father narrated to us that he heard al-Harith ibn Abi Dirar al-Khuzai say: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he called me to Islam, and I entered it and affirmed it, then he called me to zakah and I affirmed it, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shall return to my people and call them to Islam and payment of zakah, and whoever responds to me I shall collect his zakah, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, will send a messenger to me at such and such a time, so that what I collected of zakah may come to you; when al-Harith collected the zakah from those who responded to him and the time which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wanted to send to him arrived, the messenger was withheld from him and did not come to him, so al-Harith thought that displeasure from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and His Messenger had occurred concerning him, so he called the chiefs of his people and said to them: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had set a time for me to send his messenger to me to take what was with me of zakah, and breaking a promise is not of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I see the withholding of his messenger only as displeasure that occurred, so let us go and come to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent al-Walid ibn Uqbah to al-Harith to take what was with him of what he had collected of zakah, and when al-Walid set out until he reached part of the way, he became afraid and returned, and he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, al-Harith withheld the zakah from me and wanted to kill me, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, dispatched troops to al-Harith; then al-Harith came forward with his companions, when the troops set out from Madinah and he met them, al-Harith met them, and they said: This is al-Harith, and when he came upon them he said to them: To whom were you sent, they said: To you, he said: And why, they said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had sent to you al-Walid ibn Uqbah, and he claimed that you withheld the zakah from him and wanted to kill him, he said: No, by the One who sent Muhammad with the truth, I never saw him at all, nor did he come to me; and when al-Harith entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Did you withhold the zakah and want to kill my messenger, he said: No, by the One who sent you with the truth, I neither saw him nor did he come to me, and I only came forward when the messenger of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was withheld from me, fearing that displeasure from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and His Messenger had occurred; he said: Then Surah al-Hujurat was revealed: O you who believe, if a corrupt man comes to you with news, verify it, lest you strike a people in ignorance and become regretful for what you did, up to this place: as a bounty from Allah and a favor, and Allah is Knowing, Wise."
